    "body": "@annevk thanks, just to clarify as I'm not that up to date on the service worker interaction, so does that mean using a service worker in the example above would effectively cause different resolution semantics for relative imports?\n\n@domenic the intent of a `3xx` is to redirect. The current implementation does not satisfy this intent, as if it were a true redirect, it would not result in duplicate execution, it would result in a module registry entry at the redirected location. I'm not asking to change the platform semantics, I'm just asking if there's ways to make it behave as a true redirect, and if not why it is implemented at all, as it seems like a footgun.\n",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
